# Caporici Labs standards

Read `PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` before changing UI or content.

## Diátaxis

Every automotivo article MUST set `tipoDiataxis` to exactly one of:

- `explanation` — understand why / model mental (default for foundations)
- `tutorial` — learning-oriented guided lesson that creates a successful first experience
- `howto` — task-oriented steps for a competent reader with a real goal
- `reference` — factual, complete, low-interpretation technical description

Do not mix types on one page. Link across types instead.

## Markdown / MDX

- Prefer Markdown prose. Use MDX only for approved primitives: `Note`, `Tip`, `Warning`, `Danger`.
- Blank line before/after headings, lists, tables, code fences, and callouts.
- No raw HTML callouts (`div class="obs"`). No emoji-as-icons.
- Escape literal `{` / `<` in MDX when they are text, not JSX.
- Code fences need a language tag (`text` if none fits).
- Portuguese first. On first use of a technical term, give Portuguese then English original.

## Editorial contract

Frontmatter must include: titulo, resumo, trilha, ordem, nivel, status, tipoDiataxis, objetivos, fontes, limitacoes, revisao, atualizadoEm.

- `fontes[].tipo`: `norma` | `documentacao` | `pratica` | `secundaria`
- Paid standards: mark clearly; never pretend line-by-line consultation without it
- Optional `laboratorio` is an idea, not a shipped repo promise
- Production publishes only `status: publicado`

## UI / Impeccable craft floor (project-specific)

- Mode: docs/articles = Read; home = Persuade-lite that still reads as documentation
- No purple gradients, glass stacks, metric-stat heroes, icon-card IA
- No gradient text; no thick colored left borders as callout identity
- Headings carry weight — avoid eyebrow/kicker labels above H1 in articles
- Interactive elements need hover + `:focus-visible`
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Keep measure ~68ch; IBM Plex Sans + JetBrains Mono

## Voice

Developer-to-developer, calm, precise. Authorship may use first person. Never course-funnel or coach tone.

When polishing prose, use `.cursor/skills/humanizer/` with `humanizer-context.md` (`--voice technical --purpose technical`). Prefer commas/colons over em-dash saturation.
